606
00:31:41.539 --> 00:31:45.440
Because like Elaine said, her parents was from down east, too.

607
00:31:45.440 --> 00:31:52.887
<v ROBINSON>When they started doing these plants, a lot of them came here to work in the industry and in the construction.

608
00:31:52.887 --> 00:31:58.560
Because like Sulphur, I’m from Sulphur, they didn’t have nothing there but a little train station.

609
00:31:58.560 --> 00:32:03.879
I can remember the old days when I was little they had very few places.

610
00:32:03.879 --> 00:32:06.362
They didn’t have all these grocery stores.

611
00:32:06.362 --> 00:32:08.489
They had one little grocery store.

612
00:32:08.489 --> 00:32:10.262
Maybe two little gas stations.

613
00:32:10.262 --> 00:32:12.745
It was just an open field like . . .

614
00:32:12.745 --> 00:32:17.000
<v GAUTHIA>And she used to go to school in Mossville too, Elaine.

615
00:32:17.000 --> 00:32:17.258
<v ROBINSON>[Agrees].

616
00:32:17.258 --> 00:32:19.839
I went here when I was in the seventh grade.

617
00:32:19.839 --> 00:32:20.871
<v ARSENEAULT>What year was that?

618
00:32:20.871 --> 00:32:21.387
<v ROBINSON>Seventh grade.

619
00:32:21.387 --> 00:32:22.677
<v ARSENEAULT>Do you remember the year?

620
00:32:22.677 --> 00:32:25.000
Judy Gauthia-Montgomery and Elaine Robinson 4700.2615 T4569 31

621
00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:31.643
<v ROBINSON>Oh, no. not right off, but I went there in the seventh and eighth grade and I had . . . The seventh grade.

